       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.          SRCVEXEC.
       AUTHOR.              LYNN M BUNN / B WINTER.
       DATE-WRITTEN.        APRIL 15, 1979.
       DATE-COMPILED.
       INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
      *************************************************************
      *************************************************************
      **                     S R C V E X E C                     **
      *D     A RECEIVING SLIP FOR ALL ITEMS IS CREATED AND       **
      *D     ALL ASSOCIATED ENTRIES IN THE DATABASE ARE UPDATED. **
      **                                                         **
      **                PROCESSING OUTLINE                       **
      **    1.  THE FIRST SCREEN REQUESTS WHICH ITEMS TO RECEIVE **
      **    2.  THE ITEMS ARE VALIDATED.                         **
      **    3.  THE ITEMS ARE STORED IN A TABLE TO BE            **
      **          PROCESSED LATER ONE AT A TIME.                 **
      **    4.  THE SECOND SCREEN REQUESTS RECEIVED QTY AND UM.  **
      **    5.  THE QUANTITY AND UM ARE VALIDATED.               **
      **    6.  SUBPROGRAM "SFREIGHT" IS CALLED TO PROCESS       **
      **          FREIGHT DATA.  UPDATES DPOFREIGHT AND          **
      **          MSTORERM DATASETS.  WRITES A 350 AND 352       **
      **          TRANSACTION TO DDAILYTC DATASET.               **
      **    7.  UPDATES DATABASE:                                **
      **        A)  DDAILYTC - PUT     TRANSACTION 323 OR 423    **
      **                               TRANSACTION 326           **
      **        B)  DPOITEM  - UPDATE  QTY & DATE DLVR (ACCUM)   **
      **        C)  DRCVITEM  - PUT     NEW RECEIVING SLIP        **
      **        D)  DVENDITM - PUT     IF DOES NOT ALREADY EXIST **
      **                     - UPDATE  LEAD TIME                 **
      **        E)  MSTORERM - UPDATE  ONORDER, UNPAID QTY       **
      **    8.  DIRECT DELIVERY ITEM UPDATES:                    **
      **        A)  DPOITEM  - UPDATE  QTY STORED, DATE STORED   **
      **        B)  DRCVITEM  - PUT     QTY STORED, DATE STORED   **
      **        B)  USAGEFIL - KSAM    MONTH-TO-DATE USAGE       **
      **    9.  RAW MATERIALS:                                   **
      **        A)  MSTORERM - UPDATE  ONORDER WITH TOTAL DLVR   **
      **   10.  "C" PURCHASE ORDERS:                             **
      **          IF RCVR HAS A DIFFERENT PRICE UM THAN          **
      **          ORDERED UM, THEN UPDATE:                       **
      **        A)  DDAILYTC - PUT    TRANSACTION 327            **
      **   11.  PRINT THE RECEIVING SLIP.                        **
      *************************************************************
      *C***********************************************************
      *C MAY 21, 1992  -  JEFF BUNGO   (005979)                   *
      *C      CHANGED THE LINKAGE SECTION, PROCEDURE DIVISION     *
      *C      USING STATEMENT, AND THE PARAMETERS TO CALL CRSPRT  *
      *C      TO ALLOW THE PASSING OF THE MMISA BASE FROM TUDCDOCK*
      *C      AND TO CRSPRT.  THIS WAS DONE TO ALLOW CRSPRT       *
      *C      TO ACCESS AN MMISA DATABASE FILE (PER-PERSONNEL).   *
      *C SEPTEMBER 24, 1992 - JEFF BUNGO (006264)                 *
      *C      ADDED CODE TO READ DPOITEM FOR THE COMPANY CODE     *
      *C      AND WRITE TRANSACTION 326 IS THE PLANT SWITCH IS    *
      *C      IS ON FOR THIS TRANSACTION.  THE SWITCH IS PASSED   *
      *C      FROM TUDCDOCK.                                      *
      *C NOVEMBER 2, 1992   - JEFF BUNGO                          *
      *C      ADD TWO MORE VARIABLES TO PASS TO SUBPROGRAM        *
      *C      SFREIGHT.  PASS SORT-TABLE AND RAW-MATERIAL-GROUP,  *
      *C APRIL 20, 1993 - JEFF BUNGO                              *
      *C      ADDED A VARIABLE MORE-ITEMS-SAVE TO INDICATE IF THE *
      *C      THE MORE-ITEMS FLAG WAS SET FOR THE LAST SET OF     *
      *C      ITEMS PROCESSED AND RESET TO N.  THIS FLAG WILL BE  *
      *C      USED TO DETIRMINE WHETHER OR NOT TO TRY TO DELETE   *
      *C      THE REFERBACK FREIGHT RECORD FOR MORE THAN 12 ITEMS *
      *C      WHEN EXITING AND NOT PROCESSING THE NEXT SET OF     *
      *C      12 ITEMS.  THIS REFER BACK RECORD WAS CREATED IN    *
      *C      SFREIGHT.                                           *
      *C
      *C  DECEMBER 16, 1993 - JEFF BUNGO (6454)
      *C      ADDED CODE TO PREVENT A PO TO HAVE A FREIGHT
      *C      REFERBACK TO ITSELF.  THE 6 ADDITIONAL PO'S ARE
      *C      EDITTED SO THAT THEY MAY NOT MATCH THE FIRST PO
      *C      ENTERED.
      *C
      *C 27JAN1994    DAVE PLUM    REQUEST #6465 (94-004)
      *C      ADDED LOGIC IN AN ATTEMPT TO INSURE THAT THE PO
      *C      CURRENCY CODE WILL ALWAYS BE MOVED TO FIELD
      *C      "TC323-CURRENCY-CODE" OR "TC423-CURRENCY-CODE" FOR
      *C      ASHEBORO (PLANT 155).
      *C
      *C FEB 28, 1995  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      REMOVED LOGIC TO UPDATE STR-ONORDER IN MSTORERM.
      *C      THIS FIELD HAS NOT BEEN USED FOR MANY YEARS (NOW
      *C      CALCULATED FROM DPOITEM) BUT THIS PROGRAM WAS
      *C      NEVER UPDATED TO REFLECT THIS.
      *C
      *C JUN 19, 1995  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      WRITE A TC923 AFTER A TC323 WHENEVER THE DELIVERED
      *C      QUANTITY HAS A DECIMAL VALUE AND WAS ROUNDED ON THE
      *C      TC323.
      *C
      *C AUG 10, 1995  JEFF BUNGO 95-020
      *C      CALL PGM MCXSNDMSG TO SNDUSRMSG TO A USERID FOUND
      *C      ON A REQUISTION TO NOTIFY THE REQUISITIONER THAT
      *C      THE MATERIAL THAT THEY HAVE REQUESTED HAS ARRIVED
      *C      AT THE DOCK.
      *C
      *C AUG 22, 1995  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      ADDED A CALL TO CSIS PROGRAM BXRAWBAR PASSING
      *C      CODE, QTY AND UM.  THAT PROGRAM WILL THEN SUBMIT
      *C      A JOB THAT WILL RUN A NON CSIS PROGRAM TO PRINT
      *C      BAR CODES FOR RAW MATERIALS.
      *C
      *C JUNE 6, 1996  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      CHECK DOCK-SPECIAL-PRINT PARM FOR CALL THE THE
      *C      RECEIVING SLIP PRINT PROGRAM.  IF SET TO Y THEN
      *C      PRINT USING ESCAPE SEQUENCES.
      *C
      *C JULY 2, 1996  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      UPDATED LOGIC FOR THE 326 TRANSACTION.  THE TC
      *C      NUMBER WAS NOT BEING WRITTEN ON THIS TRANS AND
      *C      CAUSING A DOUBLE 323 TRANS FOR EACH ITEM.
      *C
      *C DECEMBER 4, 1996  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      IF PO ITEM RECEIVED AGAINST IS QS9000 TRACKING
      *C      THEN UPDATE FIRST AVAILABLE TRACKING ENTRY WITH
      *C      DLVR QTY, DATE, RS NUMBER, AND CARRIER.  PASS
      *C      CARRIER BACK FROM CALL TO SFREIGHT.  ALSO CHECK
      *C      IF CARRIER IS AN EXPEDITE FREIGHT CARRIER AND
      *C      SET FLAG ON TRACKING RECORD IS NECESSARY.
      *C
      *C FEBRUARY 3, 1997   JEFF BUNGO
      *C      MOVED CALL TO BXRAWBAR TO AFTER UPDATE OF DDAILYTC
      *C      MSTORERM AND USAGEFIL.  WHEN THEIR PROGRAM HAS A
      *C      PROBLEM AND THEY CANCEL, TRANSACTIONS ARE NOT WRITTEN
      *C      ONHAND AND USAGE ARE NOT UPDATED.
      *C
      *C MARCH 11, 1997 JEFF BUNGO
      *C      FIXED PROBLEM WITH RS ITEMS > 12.  THE REFERBACK TO
      *C      ORIGINAL 12 FREIGHT WAS NOT WORKING PROPERLY.
      *C
      *C APRIL 30, 1997 JEFF BUNGO
      *C      CHANGED PROGRAM TO ALLOW RECEIPT BY VERIFYING A
      *C      PREVIOUSLY RECEIVED ASN THAT HAS ALREADY SET UP
      *C      A RECEIVER.  THE ASN QTY WILL BE DISPLAYED FOR
      *C      EACH ITEM TO BE VERIFIED, AND THE FREIGHT INFORMATION
      *C      WILL BE DISPLAYED ALSO FOR VERIFICATION.  A NEW
      *C      PARAMETER WILL BE PASSED TO THIS PROGRAM TO INDICATE
      *C      THE RECEIVER ASN.  IF BLANK THEN IT IS BUSINESS AS
      *C      USUAL.  IF THE ITEM IS AN AUTO STORE ITEM AND THE
      *C      ITEM IS A FRANCHISE ITEM, THEN AUTOSTORE INTO THE
      *C      FRANCHISE PRIMARY BIN INSTEAD OF THE FIRST BIN.
      *C      THIS PROGRAM MUST ALSO PASS THE NEW PARM AS A NEW
      *C      PARM TO SFREIGHT.
      *C
      *C SEPTEMBER 3, 1997  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      IF STORES RECEIPTS INTERFACE WITH AN EXTERNAL
      *C      SYSTEM (APPLICATION) AND ALL MATERIAL IS TO BE
      *C      AUTOSTORED (BASED ON MPLTINFO KEY SRX), THEN
      *C      MARK CODE AS AUTO STORE.  THEN CALL THE EXTERNAL
      *C      INTERFACE PROGRAM TO PASS THE DATA (RECEIVER,
      *C      ITEM NUMBER, CODE, QTY, UM, DATE, AND TIME).
      *C
      *C OCT 27, 1997       CA YODER
      *C      CALL PGM MCXSNDMSG TO SNDUSRMSG TO A USERID FOUND
      *C      ON THE PO ITEM TO NOTIFY THE USER THAT THE MATERIAL
      *C      HAS ARRIVED AT THE DOCK.
      *C
      *C 11/10/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C      REMOVE SORT-TABLE OF MAX OF 12 ITEMS. USE A SUBFILE
      *C      TO HOLD ALL ITEMS ON A RECEIVING SLIP ELIMINATING THE
      *C      MAXIMUM ON NUMBER OF ITEMS.  SUBFILE RECORD WILL BE
      *C      MOVED INTO OLD SORT RECORD SD- FOR USE IN PROGRAM.
      *C
      *C 11/11/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C      CLEANED UP SOURCE CODE BY REMOVING OLD COMMENTED CODE.
      *C      REMOVE ALL REFERENCES TO LOCKING AND UNLOCKING
      *C      DATASETS, DATASET REFERENCES (FROM HP DAYS).
      *C
      *C  11/25/97    JEFF BUNGO   REQ #97-017
      *C     ADD USAGE FIELDS FOR DIRECT DELIVERY.  DD USAGE
      *C     TO BE STORED IN ADDITIONAL FIELD AND TOTAL USAGE.
      *C     STORE ISSUE USAGE CALCULATED BY TOTAL USAGE - DD USAGE.
      *C     AFTER RECEIVING A DIRECT DELIVERY ITEM, INCREMENT THE
      *C     DD USAGE FOR THE CODE IN ADDITION TO THE TOTAL USAGE.
      *C
      *C  03/10/98    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     ADD ONE LINE OF ADDITIONAL PO ITEM DESCRIPTION FOR
      *C     CODED ITEMS WHEN CODE DESCRIPTION DISPLAYED ON SCREEN.
      *C
      *C  09/24/98    CA YODER
      *C     ADDED LOGIC TO SEND AN E-MAIL MESSAGE TO BUYER ON PO
      *C     WHEN NAFTA PAPERS ARE NOT INCLUDED WITH SHIPMENT.
      *C     THIS IS FOR MEXICO ONLY.
      *C
      *C  12/18/98    CA YODER
      *C     REMOVED LOGIC TO SKIP OVERSHIPMENT CHECK FOR ASN
      *C     RECEIPTS.  DANVILLE WANTED THE CHECK RETURNED TO
      *C     THE PROCESSING OF ASNS.
      *C
      *C  09/23/99    CA YODER    UNC REQUEST
      *C     ADDED RECEIVING SLIP # TO PARAMETERS PASSED TO PROGRAM
      *C     BXRAWBAR.
      *C
      *C  04/04/02    CA YODER
      *C     BLOCKED ENTRY OF RECEIVING SLIPS FOR "999" ORDERS.
      *C
      *C  04/18/02    CA YODER    (NAPANEE REQUEST)
      *C     ADDED CALL TO "SRCVDESC" TO SHOW COMPLETE RECEIVING
      *C     SLIP ITEM DESCRIPTION.
      *C
      *C  04/29/03    CA YODER    (NAPANEE REQUEST)
      *C     SEND SECOND NOTIFICATION MESSAGE TO EXPEDITE USER IF
      *C     AN ENTRY FOR THE REQ EXISTS IN MCFPCSRQNO FILE.
      *C
      *C  07/10/03    CA YODER    (NAPANEE REQUEST)
      *C     ADDED LOGIC TO CAPTURE USER-ID OF PERSON CREATING
      *C     THE RECEIVING SLIP.
      *C
      *C  07/14/04    CA YODER    (NAPANEE REQUEST)
      *C     ADDED FIRST LINE OF REQ DESCRIPTION TO REQ NOTIFY
      *C     MESSAGE.
      *C
      *C***********************************************************
